      "quote": "Astana, Kazakhstan ahvarol@nu.edu.kz datasets for both mono and multilingual TTS. Such datasets can be constructed based on automatic speech recognition (ASR) data, like LibriTTS [7] or LibriTTS-R [8], a new version of LibriTTS with improved sound quality and 585 hours of transcribed speech from more than 2,400 speakers. Alternatively, the data for TTS datasets can be obtained by recording narration of different texts, as done for LJ- Speech [9]."
    },
    {
      "ref": 2,
      "quote": "We aim to tackle this issue in two steps, first by introducing the TatarTTS Corpus, a novel dataset for TTS in the Tatar language and then training TTS models using TatarTTS."
    },
    {
      "ref": 2,
      "quote": "The primary contributions of this work include: • Introduction of a new TTS dataset for the Tatar language."
    },
    {
      "ref": 2,
      "quote": "We aim to tackle this issue in two steps, first by introducing the TatarTTS Corpus, a novel dataset for TTS in the Tatar language and then training TTS models using TatarTTS."
    }
  ],
  "status": "answer",
  "answer": "The open voice dataset for a Turkic language was created by introducing a new TTS dataset for the Tatar language [2]. It was constructed using either automatic speech recognition (ASR) data like LibriTTS [7] or LibriTTS-R [8], which has 585 hours of transcribed speech from more than 2,400 speakers, or by recording narration of different texts as done for LJ-Speech [9] [2].",
  "clarification": ""
}

